context:
DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/deployment-groups/{group_id}
Deletes a deployment group. Associated policies no longer apply and devices stop receiving version targets. This endpoint is in Beta.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/physical-devices/{device_id}
Deletes a WARP device.
Required: device_id (path); account_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/ip-profiles/{profile_id}
Delete a WARP Device IP profile.
Required: account_id (path); profile_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/registrations/{registration_id}
Deletes a WARP registration.
Required: registration_id (path); account_id (path)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/networks/{network_id}
Deletes a device managed network and fetches a list of the remaining device managed networks for an account.
Required: network_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/networks/{network_id}
Fetches details for a single managed network.
Required: network_id (path); account_id (path)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/networks/{network_id}
Updates a configured device managed network.
Required: network_id (path); account_id (path); body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/integration/{integration_id}
Delete a configured device posture integration.
Required: integration_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/integration/{integration_id}
Fetches details for a single device posture integration.
Required: integration_id (path); account_id (path)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/integration/{integration_id}
Updates a configured device posture integration.
Required: integration_id (path); account_id (path); body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/{rule_id}
Deletes a device posture rule.
Required: rule_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/{rule_id}
Fetches a single device posture rule.
Required: rule_id (path); account_id (path)

PUT /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/posture/{rule_id}
Updates a device posture rule.
Required: rule_id (path); account_id (path); body (body)

DELETE /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/policy/{policy_id}
Deletes a device settings profile and fetches a list of the remaining profiles for an account.
Required: policy_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/{device_id}
Fetches a single WARP device. Not supported when [multi-user mode](https://developers.cloudflare.com/cloudflare-one/connections/connect-devices/warp/deployment/mdm-deployment/windows-multiuser/) is enabled for the account. **Deprecated**: please use one of the following endpoints instead: - GET /accounts/{account_id}/devices/physical-devices/{device_id} - GET /accounts/{account_id}/devices/registrations/{registration_id}
Required: device_id (path); account_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/policy/{policy_id}
Fetches a device settings profile by ID.
Required: policy_id (path); account_id (path)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/policy/{policy_id}
Updates a configured device settings profile.
Required: policy_id (path); account_id (path); body (body)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/deployment-groups/{group_id}
Fetches a single deployment group by its ID. This endpoint is in Beta.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path)

GET /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/ip-profiles/{profile_id}
Fetches a single WARP Device IP profile.
Required: account_id (path); profile_id (path)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/deployment-groups/{group_id}
Updates a deployment group. Returns 409 if any newly added policy IDs already belong to another deployment group. This endpoint is in Beta.
Required: account_id (path); group_id (path); body (body)

PATCH /client/v4/accounts/{account_id}/devices/ip-profiles/{profile_id}
Updates a WARP Device IP profile. Currently, only IPv4 Device subnets can be associated.
Required: account_id (path); profile_id (path); body (body)
